/*  showGen -- GX-6, THE LOOKSEE. Run it and read the generated parse method.

    NO PREPARATION: no environment variable, no shell, no arguments. Open it in
    Xcode, run, read the output. The capture arms itself with recordParse()
    below, which is the in-fixture door onto the same gate INCANT_PARSE_RECORD
    opens. Nothing is written to disk.

    TO LOOK AT A DIFFERENT RULE, EDIT THE ONE MARKED LINE. Incant fixtures are
    invoked as `incant <file>` with no argument channel, so the name cannot come
    from outside -- but GA (2026-08-06) taught genParse and showParse to accept
    a FIELD that resolves to text, so the name is written once here and used
    twice below, and the two calls cannot drift apart.

    THE `=` IS LOAD-BEARING. `gsRule = "Parens";` gives the field data;
    `gsRule "Parens";` does NOT -- that form prints as `gsRule`, measured --
    and genParse would then refuse a rule by that name. Bear-trap #26 wearing
    define syntax.

    GENERATION ONLY. No install, no contact with incant/grammar, cannot move a
    baseline: genParse emits and installs nothing, and the ParsE record is gated
    off unless a fixture arms it.

    The twelve plannable rules are: Braced Parens ElsE InvokE InvokeArg
    PrintField WardeD GrouP CodE RunRulE BlocK ExpressioN.  */
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking UnitTests Utilities list;

registry(cOMMANDs);
define genParse immediateAction=genParse; ;
define showParse immediateAction=showParse; ;
define recordParse immediateAction=recordParse; ;

register(ShowGen);
define
    gsRule = "Parens";
    ;

recordParse();
genParse(gsRule);
print "---- generated method ----":;
showParse(gsRule);
print "SHOWGEN SENTINEL":;
stop();
